Third-party material NOT covered by the Apache License
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

worker-shared/apple-roots.js contains two X.509 root certificates published by Apple
Inc.: "Apple Root CA - G2" and "Apple Root CA - G3", stored as base64-encoded DER.

Those certificates are the property of Apple Inc. They are reproduced here unmodified,
as public cryptographic trust anchors, so that App Store purchase receipts can be
verified offline against a pinned root rather than one fetched at runtime. They are
obtained from Apple's public certificate authority page:

    https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/

No licence to those certificates is granted by this project, and none is claimed over
them. They are not a contribution to this work within the meaning of the Apache License,
and nothing in that License applies to them. Redistribution of public root certificates
is ordinary practice: every operating system, browser and language runtime ships a
comparable set.

If you fork this project, do not treat those values as source code to be edited. Rotating
them means downloading the current certificates from Apple and replacing them wholesale,
in both workers at once, as the file's own header explains.

